4. Required Reading (Papers)

Drop these names in your README.md or during an interview.

    For the Scoring Logic:

        📄 Paper: "Phone-level pronunciation scoring and assessment for interactive language learning" (Witt & Young).

        Key Concept: GOP (Goodness of Pronunciation). This is the industry standard for scoring.

    For the "zh/sh/r" Feature:

        📄 Paper: "Golden Mandarin (I)—A real-time mandarin speech dictation machine" (Lin-Shan Lee et al.).

        Key Concept: Using Cepstral Coefficients (MFCCs) to classify Mandarin initials.

    For the Tone Sandhi Rules:

        📄 Topic: Look for papers on "Mandarin Tone Sandhi Disambiguation."

        In Your Code: You currently use simple if/else rules in core/generator.py. Real systems use "Conditional Random Fields" (CRF) to predict these changes.
